@startuml
title MCPVault components and authority boundaries
node "Approved host" {
  component "Codex / existing client" as Client
  component "Five MCP tools" as MCP
  component "Endpoint registry" as Registry
  component "Knowledge / retrieval / publication services" as Services
  component "Filesystem + PathFilter + current access policy" as Boundary
  database "Disposable indexes / metadata / semantic cache" as Cache
  component "Opt-in host-only Graphify" as Graphify
  database "Explicit source allowlist + private derived cache" as CodeCache
  database "Verified private work receipts / checkpoints" as Journal
  Client --> MCP
  MCP --> Registry
  Registry --> Services
  Services --> Boundary
  Services --> Cache : discovery only
  Services --> Journal : explicit separate host grant only
  Graphify --> CodeCache : pinned local AST; no model provider
  Graphify ..> Client : structural candidates, not test evidence
}
node "NAS" {
  database "Authoritative Markdown / Properties / source bytes" as Vault
}
Boundary --> Vault : bounded revision-safe reads / guarded writes
Vault ..> Cache : rebuildable read model
note bottom of MCP
  orient_wiki, get_agent_pulse, list_active_capabilities,
  search_capabilities, call_endpoint
end note
note bottom of Vault
  Source preservation, live data and rollback remain separate obligations.
  Application guards do not prove NAS direct-write protection.
end note
note bottom of Graphify
  No graph DB, RDF server, external renderer or public writer.
  Neither caches nor model names grant access or execution permission.
end note
@enduml
